-- title:
--   Dimension criterion for a single element to generate a finite algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $A$ be a finite-dimensional commutative $K$-algebra, and let $x\in A$. Suppose the subalgebra $K[x]$ generated by $x$ has dimension $n$, and write $d=\dim_K A$. Polynomial evaluation uses the specified $K$-algebra structure on $A$.
--
--   Then $n\le d$, and the following are equivalent:
--
--   - $n=d$;
--   - $K[x]=A$;
--   - the evaluation map $K[T]\to A$, $q\mapsto q(x)$, is surjective.
--
--   Moreover,
--   $$
--   n<d\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
--   \text{there exists }y\in A\text{ such that }q(x)\ne y\text{ for every }q\in K[T].
--   $$
--   Thus a strict dimension deficit is precisely failure of $x$ to generate the whole algebra.
--
--   The finite-dimensionality of the ambient algebra is an explicit hypothesis. The field may have any characteristic, and trivial target algebras are included. No assertion that every element generates $A$ is made.
-- source:
--   Derived supporting algebra lemma for the Senthil Kumar mission. At Mathlib revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474, Submodule.eq_top_of_finrank_eq is in LinearAlgebra/FiniteDimensional/Basic.lean lines 70-86; Algebra.adjoin_singleton_eq_range_aeval is in RingTheory/Adjoin/Polynomial/Basic.lean lines 52-54; Algebra.toSubmodule_eq_top and AlgHom.range_eq_top are in Algebra/Algebra/Subalgebra/Lattice.lean lines 82-83 and 251-253. Primary documentation: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/FiniteDimensional/Basic.html#Submodule.eq_top_of_finrank_eq and https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/Adjoin/Polynomial/Basic.html#Algebra.adjoin_singleton_eq_range_aeval . If A is a finite-dimensional commutative K-algebra and K[x] has dimension n, then n is at most dim_K(A), with equality exactly when x generates A, equivalently when polynomial evaluation at x is surjective. Strict inequality is equivalent to existence of an element of A that is not any polynomial in x. Any field characteristic and trivial target algebras are allowed. Ambient finite-dimensionality is an explicit essential hypothesis. No platform theorem dependencies or new definitions.

import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Adjoin.Polynomial.Basic

theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.adjoin_dimension_generation_criterion
    (K A : Type*) [Field K] [CommRing A] [Algebra K A] [FiniteDimensional K A]
    (x : A) (n d : ℕ) (hdim : Module.finrank K (Algebra.adjoin K ({x} : Set A)) = n)
    (hdimA : Module.finrank K A = d) :
    n ≤ d ∧
      (n = d ↔ Algebra.adjoin K ({x} : Set A) = ⊤) ∧
      (n = d ↔
        Function.Surjective (fun q : Polynomial K => q.eval₂ (algebraMap K A) x)) ∧
      (n < d ↔
        ∃ y : A, ∀ q : Polynomial K, q.eval₂ (algebraMap K A) x ≠ y) := by sorry
